From ae32d71003117fa92ab5fb5c10bef6ce359c166d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:11:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Android: model and Effort chips in the Claude chat header (as
 on the Mac)

- the chat's model, then its effort: only the levels the model takes, "(default)" on the model's own; effort hides for a
  model without it; nothing shows before GET /v1/claude/models answers (or on an older server)
- per chat (PATCH /v1/claude/chats/:id {model}/{effort}; null clears), the last effort choice for new chats
- chips sit in a row already there (title, else the chat list row, else the status line): embedded chats keep their space
- MuseMenu: an item with icon "" draws none (picker lists check only the chosen row)
- ClaudeEffortTest (rules, store, HTTP bodies) and screenshot state claude_<theme>_model_effort_<390|360>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Py2rxnJMgrcJzBU2H7pwjQ
